{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43788538",
      "title": "Introducing Signals",
      "lectureOrder": 29,
      "videoOrder": 25,
      "sourceHash": "60b4b4040968eaaa68bba81c8909a2be145013dbd5da7f24f65630543c70dc1a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.27,
          "end": 3.48,
          "en": "So we did now take a closer look at State",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.48,
          "end": 6.57,
          "en": "and how we can change State with Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.57,
          "end": 8.97,
          "en": "over the last lectures.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.97,
          "end": 12.45,
          "en": "Now it is worth noting that this way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.45,
          "end": 16.2,
          "en": "of updating the State of the application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.2,
          "end": 18.93,
          "en": "and of the user interface, therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.93,
          "end": 22.08,
          "en": "is just one way of doing it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.08,
          "end": 24.63,
          "en": "And it is the way that has been around",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.63,
          "end": 27.18,
          "en": "since the release of Angular 2",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.18,
          "end": 29.58,
          "en": "because it is pretty straightforward",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.58,
          "end": 32.07,
          "en": "and easy to use and understand.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.07,
          "end": 36.54,
          "en": "It is however, not the only way of changing data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.54,
          "end": 38.67,
          "en": "that should have an impact on the UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.67,
          "end": 40.83,
          "en": "because there is a newer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.83,
          "end": 43.53,
          "en": "more recent mechanism available as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.53,
          "end": 46.47,
          "en": "which I also wanna show you here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.47,
          "end": 50.13,
          "en": "And that mechanism uses a concept called Signals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.13,
          "end": 53.07,
          "en": "which in the end are special kinds of values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.07,
          "end": 55.56,
          "en": "that tell Angular when they change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.56,
          "end": 57.33,
          "en": "And I'll show you how to work with them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.33,
          "end": 59.19,
          "en": "and I'll also thereafter explain",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.19,
          "end": 60.93,
          "en": "why you might wanna use them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 60.93,
          "end": 64.413,
          "en": "instead of this other mechanism I showed you before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.34,
          "end": 68.25,
          "en": "You create such a Signal value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 68.25,
          "end": 72.48,
          "en": "by importing the Signal function from Angular core,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.48,
          "end": 74.133,
          "en": "so that's the first step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.75,
          "end": 79.77,
          "en": "With that imported, you then create such a Signal value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.77,
          "end": 82.19,
          "en": "and store it in a property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.19,
          "end": 84.78,
          "en": "of your component class component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 84.78,
          "end": 86.76,
          "en": "In our case, where I wanna replace",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 86.76,
          "end": 90.87,
          "en": "this selected user property value with such a Signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.87,
          "end": 92.49000000000001,
          "en": "I'll simply create it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 92.49000000000001,
          "end": 94.59,
          "en": "on the right side of this equal sign here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 95.52000000000001,
          "end": 98.55,
          "en": "You can then also pass an initial value to the Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 98.55,
          "end": 102.12,
          "en": "And here I'll pass that user object to the Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.12,
          "end": 104.37,
          "en": "So that initial user object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.37,
          "end": 107.163,
          "en": "which we get with help of this random index.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.14,
          "end": 113.37,
          "en": "Now, the idea behind this Signal thing here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.37,
          "end": 117.33,
          "en": "is that it's in the end a container you could say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.33,
          "end": 122.31,
          "en": "that contains a value like this initial dummy user here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 122.31,
          "end": 125.52,
          "en": "And when you then change that value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.52,
          "end": 129.99,
          "en": "Angular will be notified about that change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.99,
          "end": 134.7,
          "en": "And Angular then is able to identify all the places,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.7,
          "end": 137.31,
          "en": "for example, in your templates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.31,
          "end": 140.1,
          "en": "where that value is being used.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 140.1,
          "end": 143.61,
          "en": "So where that Signal is being used in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 143.61,
          "end": 147.27,
          "en": "and it's then able to update these places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.27,
          "end": 149.13,
          "en": "And I'll show you how to read",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 149.13,
          "end": 152.73,
          "en": "and use a Signal in a template in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.73,
          "end": 154.95,
          "en": "But that's the idea behind Signals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.95,
          "end": 158.04,
          "en": "in the end, you are dealing with containers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 158.04,
          "end": 162.03,
          "en": "that contain values and that notify Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 162.03,
          "end": 164.37,
          "en": "whenever those values change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 164.37,
          "end": 168.69,
          "en": "so that Angular can then update the parts of the UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 168.69,
          "end": 170.82,
          "en": "where those values are used,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 170.82,
          "end": 174.57,
          "en": "and that can be a very efficient updating mechanism,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 174.57,
          "end": 177.183,
          "en": "but I'll get back to that in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 178.02,
          "end": 181.17,
          "en": "So therefore of the idea behind Signals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 181.17,
          "end": 184.71,
          "en": "is that you don't just have some initial values in them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 184.71,
          "end": 187.77,
          "en": "but that you can also change those values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 187.77,
          "end": 192.27,
          "en": "And you can, for example, change the value of a Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 192.27,
          "end": 196.44,
          "en": "by calling the set method on that Signal object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 196.44,
          "end": 200.07,
          "en": "so by calling this selected user set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 200.07,
          "end": 202.71,
          "en": "And by then passing the new value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 202.71,
          "end": 207.43,
          "en": "in this case, the new dummy user to that set method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 208.68,
          "end": 212.043,
          "en": "like this, and this line here can then be deleted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 213.32999999999998,
          "end": 217.14,
          "en": "So that's how we can initialize and then update a Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 217.14,
          "end": 221.13,
          "en": "We also sometimes need to read it though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 221.13,
          "end": 223.59,
          "en": "We need to extract a value from it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 223.59,
          "end": 227.823,
          "en": "for example, here where we compute the image path value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 229.05,
          "end": 233.22,
          "en": "Now, I'll get back to this computed value in just a second,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 233.22,
          "end": 237.03,
          "en": "and I'll instead start here in the user component template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 237.03,
          "end": 240.453,
          "en": "where we also try to access the Signal value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 241.65,
          "end": 243.84,
          "en": "Because when you have such a Signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 243.84,
          "end": 248.37,
          "en": "you don't access the value stored in the Signal like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 248.37,
          "end": 253.08,
          "en": "but instead you have to call the Signal value as a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 253.08,
          "end": 255.3,
          "en": "so by adding parentheses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 255.3,
          "end": 258.3,
          "en": "after the property that stores the Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 258.3,
          "end": 261.99,
          "en": "this then executes the Signal's read function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 261.99,
          "end": 263.31,
          "en": "which gives you the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 263.31,
          "end": 266.19,
          "en": "that's currently stored in the Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 266.19,
          "end": 267.84,
          "en": "So whenever you are dealing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 267.84,
          "end": 270.33,
          "en": "with a property that stores a Signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 270.33,
          "end": 274.40999999999997,
          "en": "you have to execute this property as a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 274.40999999999997,
          "end": 277.32,
          "en": "to get the latest value from it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 277.32,
          "end": 282.09000000000003,
          "en": "Now what this read here does is it tells Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 282.09000000000003,
          "end": 285.48,
          "en": "that you are trying to get the value of that Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 285.48,
          "end": 289.65,
          "en": "in this specific place here, so in this template here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 289.65,
          "end": 293.79,
          "en": "And Angular is therefore able to set up a subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 293.79,
          "end": 297.33,
          "en": "behind the scenes, which will make sure that this place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 297.33,
          "end": 299.7,
          "en": "where that Signal value is used,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 299.7,
          "end": 304.44,
          "en": "so this template in this case, will be reevaluated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 304.44,
          "end": 308.13,
          "en": "rerendered and updated on the UI you could say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 308.13,
          "end": 311.97,
          "en": "whenever that Signal value changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 311.97,
          "end": 315.09,
          "en": "So Angular sets up a tracking mechanism",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 315.09,
          "end": 318.51,
          "en": "that automatically makes sure that the UI is updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 318.51,
          "end": 322.35,
          "en": "whenever the underlying value changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 322.35,
          "end": 326.58,
          "en": "And that's different from the State management mechanism",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 326.58,
          "end": 329.19,
          "en": "we had before without Signals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 329.19,
          "end": 332.61,
          "en": "because there, when not using Signals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 332.61,
          "end": 337.61,
          "en": "Angular uses a sub package called Zone.js",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 337.65,
          "end": 341.55,
          "en": "to create so-called zones around your components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 341.55,
          "end": 345.3,
          "en": "which in the end is simply an invisible grouping mechanism",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 345.3,
          "end": 347.79,
          "en": "set up behind the scenes by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 347.79,
          "end": 350.76,
          "en": "where it listens for all kinds of events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 350.76,
          "end": 353.61,
          "en": "that could trigger State changes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 353.61,
          "end": 357.21,
          "en": "so data changes that should affect the UI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 357.21,
          "end": 359.64,
          "en": "And whenever such a trigger occurs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 359.64,
          "end": 362.31,
          "en": "because for example, a user clicked a button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 362.31,
          "end": 364.65,
          "en": "which would be one possible trigger,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 364.65,
          "end": 367.17,
          "en": "whenever that happens, Angular goes ahead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 367.17,
          "end": 370.41,
          "en": "and checks all the Components in that zone",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 370.41,
          "end": 373.5,
          "en": "to find out whether some data changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 373.5,
          "end": 376.11,
          "en": "that now needs to be updated on the UI,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 376.11,
          "end": 380.07,
          "en": "so whether the UI needs to be updated in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 380.07,
          "end": 382.29,
          "en": "That's how Angular performs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 382.29,
          "end": 385.53,
          "en": "that change detection without Signals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 385.53,
          "end": 388.23,
          "en": "and the advantage of Signals is that Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 388.23,
          "end": 393.23,
          "en": "could get rid of Zone.js and this zone concept.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 393.84000000000003,
          "end": 397.29,
          "en": "So it allows Angular to perform change detection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 397.29,
          "end": 400.293,
          "en": "and UI updating in a more efficient manner.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 401.79,
          "end": 405.3,
          "en": "That's why this Signal based change detection",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 405.3,
          "end": 407.85,
          "en": "and State management was introduced",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 407.85,
          "end": 411.78,
          "en": "because this allows Angular to update the UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 411.78,
          "end": 414.12,
          "en": "in a more fine-grained way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 414.12,
          "end": 416.61,
          "en": "where it doesn't have to check everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 416.61,
          "end": 418.35,
          "en": "for every possible event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 418.35,
          "end": 421.113,
          "en": "that could occur anywhere in the application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 422.07,
          "end": 424.35,
          "en": "That's the idea behind Signals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 424.35,
          "end": 426.6,
          "en": "and that's why even though the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 426.6,
          "end": 430.38,
          "en": "is a bit more verbose than the code we had before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 430.38,
          "end": 433.23,
          "en": "using Signals is definitely something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 433.23,
          "end": 436.413,
          "en": "you might wanna consider when working with Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 437.34,
          "end": 440.67,
          "en": "Now all that being said, it's also worth noting though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 440.67,
          "end": 443.88,
          "en": "that this Signal feature is rather new.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 443.88,
          "end": 447.87,
          "en": "Signals were introduced with Angular 16",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 447.87,
          "end": 452.37,
          "en": "and partially became stable with Angular 17.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 452.37,
          "end": 455.7,
          "en": "And therefore, if you are working on an older code base",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 455.7,
          "end": 459.93,
          "en": "or simply with a team that's used to Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 459.93,
          "end": 464.55,
          "en": "as it always worked, Signals might not be an option there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 464.55,
          "end": 466.44,
          "en": "which is why I showed you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 466.44,
          "end": 469.59000000000003,
          "en": "that other State management approach first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 469.59000000000003,
          "end": 473.04,
          "en": "But that being said, I'll have a complete section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 473.04,
          "end": 475.68,
          "en": "about Signals later in this course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 475.68,
          "end": 478.47,
          "en": "where we will dive way deeper into Signals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 478.47,
          "end": 481.59,
          "en": "so that you are well prepared to work with Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 481.59,
          "end": 483.51,
          "en": "no matter if you are in a project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 483.51,
          "end": 485.46,
          "en": "that is able to use Signals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 485.46,
          "end": 488.58,
          "en": "which do offer advantages as I explained",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 488.58,
          "end": 492.36,
          "en": "or if you are working with Angular without Signals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 492.36,
          "end": 496.77,
          "en": "My goal with this course is to prepare you for both options",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 496.77,
          "end": 498.33,
          "en": "and give you the knowledge you need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 498.33,
          "end": 501.36,
          "en": "for both options and approaches.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 501.36,
          "end": 503.28,
          "en": "Now here in this application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 503.28,
          "end": 504.78,
          "en": "we still got a missing piece though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 504.78,
          "end": 506.64,
          "en": "and that's this image path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 506.64,
          "end": 509.16,
          "en": "Previously without Signals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 509.16,
          "end": 513.9,
          "en": "we could create a computed value with help of such a getter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 513.9,
          "end": 517.65,
          "en": "Now when using Signals, this is not how you would do it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 517.65,
          "end": 520.05,
          "en": "Instead, in a world with Signals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 520.05,
          "end": 522.39,
          "en": "you would set up such a computed value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 522.39,
          "end": 525.39,
          "en": "by simply adding another regular property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 525.39,
          "end": 527.103,
          "en": "called imagePath maybe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 528.06,
          "end": 532.17,
          "en": "And you would then use the computed function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 532.17,
          "end": 535.233,
          "en": "which is also imported from at Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 536.97,
          "end": 538.53,
          "en": "And computed is a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 538.53,
          "end": 541.23,
          "en": "that's meant to be used with Signals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 541.23,
          "end": 545.7,
          "en": "because computed then takes a function as an argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 545.7,
          "end": 550.05,
          "en": "So you pass a function to this computed function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 550.05,
          "end": 553.26,
          "en": "and this function which you pass to computed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 553.26,
          "end": 555.57,
          "en": "And here I'm simply using an arrow function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 555.57,
          "end": 557.97,
          "en": "but you could be using a regular function as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 557.97,
          "end": 561.9,
          "en": "of course, and you also don't have to define it in line",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 174,
          "start": 561.9,
          "end": 563.88,
          "en": "as I'm doing it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 175,
          "start": 563.88,
          "end": 568.2,
          "en": "but this function now should return the computed value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 176,
          "start": 568.2,
          "end": 571.17,
          "en": "which may use a Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 177,
          "start": 571.17,
          "end": 573.72,
          "en": "So in my case here, I wanna return a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 178,
          "start": 573.72,
          "end": 578.72,
          "en": "which is the combination of this fixed string, assets/users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 179,
          "start": 579.57,
          "end": 584.16,
          "en": "combined with this selected user being executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 180,
          "start": 584.16,
          "end": 587.1,
          "en": "because we wanna read that Signal value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 181,
          "start": 587.1,
          "end": 591.54,
          "en": "And in that case, as explained, you always must execute it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 182,
          "start": 591.54,
          "end": 594.93,
          "en": "And then I wanna access the avatar property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 183,
          "start": 594.93,
          "end": 598.68,
          "en": "on that user object that's stored in the Signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 184,
          "start": 598.68,
          "end": 601.11,
          "en": "and that is how you would compute a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 185,
          "start": 601.11,
          "end": 602.733,
          "en": "when using Signals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 186,
          "start": 603.63,
          "end": 607.2,
          "en": "Now, why would you create a computed value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 187,
          "start": 607.2,
          "end": 611.46,
          "en": "based on Signals like this with this computed function?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 188,
          "start": 611.46,
          "end": 615.09,
          "en": "Well, because when using this computed function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 189,
          "start": 615.09,
          "end": 619.44,
          "en": "Angular automatically analyzes whether you are reading",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 190,
          "start": 619.44,
          "end": 622.2,
          "en": "some Signal value inside of that function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 191,
          "start": 622.2,
          "end": 624.03,
          "en": "you passed to compute it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 192,
          "start": 624.03,
          "end": 628.47,
          "en": "And if that's the case, Angular again sets up a subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 193,
          "start": 628.47,
          "end": 631.11,
          "en": "to that Signal that's being used in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 194,
          "start": 631.11,
          "end": 634.05,
          "en": "so to the selected user, Signal in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 195,
          "start": 634.05,
          "end": 637.17,
          "en": "And whenever that Signal receives a new value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 196,
          "start": 637.17,
          "end": 640.39,
          "en": "and only then Angular will recompute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 197,
          "start": 641.28,
          "end": 642.78,
          "en": "the image path here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 198,
          "start": 642.78,
          "end": 646.29,
          "en": "So it's a very efficient way of setting up a computed value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 199,
          "start": 646.29,
          "end": 648.75,
          "en": "because it will not be recomputed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 200,
          "start": 648.75,
          "end": 652.11,
          "en": "every time anything changes in this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 201,
          "start": 652.11,
          "end": 654.18,
          "en": "or the overall application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 202,
          "start": 654.18,
          "end": 657,
          "en": "but instead, it will only be recomputed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 203,
          "start": 657,
          "end": 660.33,
          "en": "if one of the Signals used inside of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 204,
          "start": 660.33,
          "end": 663.33,
          "en": "So in this case, if this selected user Signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 205,
          "start": 663.33,
          "end": 667.473,
          "en": "which is the only Signal used in there, if that changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 206,
          "start": 668.34,
          "end": 672.06,
          "en": "Now you just also have to make sure that in the template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 207,
          "start": 672.06,
          "end": 675.69,
          "en": "you also execute this computed property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 208,
          "start": 675.69,
          "end": 678.693,
          "en": "because under the hood it also creates a Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 209,
          "start": 679.56,
          "end": 682.53,
          "en": "Just a Signal that will automatically update",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 210,
          "start": 682.53,
          "end": 684.99,
          "en": "whenever the Signals it depends on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 211,
          "start": 684.99,
          "end": 688.41,
          "en": "in this case, the selectedUser, change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 212,
          "start": 688.41,
          "end": 691.533,
          "en": "Angular will make sure that this is tracked automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 213,
          "start": 692.46,
          "end": 696.09,
          "en": "But since image path therefore also is a Signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 214,
          "start": 696.09,
          "end": 698.46,
          "en": "as you can also see if you hover over it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 215,
          "start": 698.46,
          "end": 702.45,
          "en": "you can see the type of the value here, it's a Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 216,
          "start": 702.45,
          "end": 705,
          "en": "Since that's the case, you have to execute it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 217,
          "start": 705,
          "end": 706.65,
          "en": "like a function in your template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 218,
          "start": 706.65,
          "end": 710.733,
          "en": "because that's always how you read those Signal values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 219,
          "start": 712.05,
          "end": 714.96,
          "en": "And with that, if you save everything and you reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 220,
          "start": 714.96,
          "end": 717.81,
          "en": "you should have the same behavior as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 221,
          "start": 717.81,
          "end": 719.22,
          "en": "In this application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 222,
          "start": 719.22,
          "end": 723.24,
          "en": "you should have this updating user item here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 223,
          "start": 723.24,
          "end": 726.12,
          "en": "but now implemented with help of Signals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 224,
          "start": 726.12,
          "end": 729.72,
          "en": "which do offer the advantage I explained before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 225,
          "start": 729.72,
          "end": 734.61,
          "en": "Now, because many Angular projects do not use Signals yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 226,
          "start": 734.61,
          "end": 737.91,
          "en": "or might not even be able to use Signals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 227,
          "start": 737.91,
          "end": 740.91,
          "en": "because they're using an older Angular version,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 228,
          "start": 740.91,
          "end": 743.61,
          "en": "I will actually not use Signals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 229,
          "start": 743.61,
          "end": 746.43,
          "en": "everywhere in this demo application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 230,
          "start": 746.43,
          "end": 748.62,
          "en": "but instead simply use them here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 231,
